# Copy to backend/.env — every value is optional; the system runs fully offline without any of them.
#
# ─── QUICK START FOR TEAMMATES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. cp backend/.env.example backend/.env     (already done if you have this file)
# 2. cd backend && python -m app.ingestion.load_demo_case
#    → Creates backend/data/cna.db (SQLite, ~50 MB) with 23,000+ entities locally.
# 3. python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload
# No database server needed. No cloud account needed. Works fully offline.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Database (SQLite by default — zero config, works offline) ---
# The db file is created at backend/data/cna.db when you run load_demo_case.py.
# Uncomment and fill in the line below only if your team uses a shared Postgres server.
# CNA_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require

# --- security (change in production) ---
CNA_JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
CNA_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin@123
CNA_BOOTSTRAP_ANALYST_PASSWORD=analyst@123

# --- optional AI enrichment (Claude). Leave unset to use the deterministic pipeline only ---
# --- LLM tier 3 (optional; the system is fully functional without any key) ---
# Served through OpenRouter by default. Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
# CNA_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
# CNA_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# CNA_LLM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free
#
# A reasoning model spends max_tokens on thinking before it answers; "none" keeps the
# budget for the structured output. Raise to low/medium for harder narrative.
# CNA_LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=none
#
# Tier-3 extraction over EVERY ingested document. Off by default: one call costs tens of
# seconds, so a few hundred documents becomes hours. The investigator and report narration
# work without this. Turn it on only for a corpus of prose worth the wait.
# CNA_LLM_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=false
#
# Direct Anthropic key instead of OpenRouter:
# CNA_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
#
# The investigator agent needs ONE of these. They are tried in the order given by
# CNA_LLM_PROVIDERS and the first that answers takes the turn, so a throttled key or a dead
# region falls through to the next instead of taking the agent down. Without any key the rest
# of the console still works fully - only the agent lens is disabled.
# CNA_GEMINI_API_KEY=            # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# CNA_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# CNA_NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...   # https://build.nvidia.com
# CNA_NVIDIA_MODEL=meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
# CNA_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CNA_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# CNA_LLM_PROVIDERS=gemini,nvidia,anthropic

# --- open web access for the agent ---
# With a Firecrawl key the agent renders JS pages and gets clean markdown; without one it falls
# back to a keyless DuckDuckGo + plain-HTTP path that still works, including from cache offline.
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...

# --- data.gov.in (NCRB / MHA statistics). Free key: https://data.gov.in/user/register
# Without it the shared sample key is used, which is heavily throttled (HTTP 429).
# CNA_DATA_GOV_IN_KEY=

# --- AI tiers ---
# Tier 2: zero-shot transformer NER (GLiNER). Needs: uv pip install -e ".[neural]"  (~2 GB PyTorch)
# Finds entity types the rules cannot express (drug substance, weapon, quantity, gang name...).
# CNA_NEURAL_NER_ENABLED=true
# CNA_NEURAL_NER_THRESHOLD=0.40
# Semantic document search (fastembed/ONNX, no PyTorch). On by default.
# CNA_SEMANTIC_SEARCH_ENABLED=true

# --- performance ---
# Force the NetworkX centrality path instead of rustworkx (A/B comparison / troubleshooting)
# CNA_DISABLE_RUSTWORKX=1

# --- behaviour ---
# Load the bundled benchmark case on first start when the database is empty (default true)
CNA_AUTOLOAD_DEMO=true
# Database (SQLite by default; any SQLAlchemy URL works, e.g. postgresql+psycopg://user:pw@host/db)
# CNA_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./data/cna.db
